# Committed CoMind artifacts are generated with LF endings on every platform.
# Without this, a Windows checkout rewrites them to CRLF and every teammate sees
# a whole-file diff the next time anyone regenerates.
#
# Scoped to *.md on purpose: `.planning/` is user-authored and may hold images
# or PDFs, and forcing text semantics on those corrupts them on checkout.
.ai-memory/**/*.md text eol=lf
.planning/**/*.md  text eol=lf
.comind/manifest.json text eol=lf
graphify-out/GRAPH_REPORT.md text eol=lf
graphify-out/graph.json text eol=lf

# graph.json is regenerated wholesale on every build, so two developers who both
# commit a graph conflict on a file no human can resolve. graphify ships a union
# merge driver for exactly this. `graphify hook install` would append this same
# line itself; its own duplicate check scans the whole file and matches on
# `<...>graph.json ... merge=graphify`, so our copy makes that append a no-op
# rather than a second line.
#
# The attribute alone is inert: the driver body is machine-local git config that
# cannot be committed. `comind setup` registers it on every machine, JOIN
# included — without that half, git reports an unknown driver and falls back to
# a plain conflict, which is worse than never having claimed one.
graphify-out/graph.json merge=graphify
